  "answer": "We should balance a chemical equation because of the law of conservation of mass. This law states that the total mass of the products formed in a chemical reaction must be equal to the total mass of the reactants consumed. Atoms are neither created nor destroyed in chemical reactions, so the number of atoms of each element must be the same on both sides of the equation. A balanced chemical equation ensures that the number of atoms of each element is equal on the reactant side (left side) and the product side (right side). This helps in accurately representing the chemical reaction and understanding the stoichiometric relationships between reactants and products.",
